<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15200" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρκτοῦρος</span></b> , ὁ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖρος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guard</i>) the star
				<i>Arcturus, Bearward</i> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				566
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				610
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxag.
				20
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the time of his heliacal rising,</i> i.e. <i>the middle of
				September,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1137
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ὥραν τὴν τοῦ τρυγᾶν Ἀρκτούρῳ
					σύνδρομον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					844e
				</span></i>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρυγητής</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> Ἀρκτούρου ἐπιτολαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.78
				</span></i>
			, etc.</div>
